    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d247">

                <pb facs="0399" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg283"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1684.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Sullivan to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-08T10:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1915—10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Political plot under way here to impeach President Jiménes on the charge that he
                    failed to act in carrying out congressional resololution to remove Johnston and
                    on further charges of frivolous nature made against Velásquez, Minister of
                    Fomento; both charges aimed at American influence here. Constitution provides
                    that majority of both Houses can impeach President. Upon such vote President
                    ipso facto loses executive power and election of new president must follow by
                    Congress. Vidal and Arias supporting plot, with the Horacistas assisting. This
                    plan offers malcontents a way to upset the Government without resorting to
                    revolution. Arias is the candidate for the presidency, supported by members of
                    Legislature who desire to shake off restrictions on looting of Government funds.
                    Several secret meetings have already been held and certain members of Cabinet
                    are said to sympathize with the project. I recommend that politicians be given
                    to understand that Jiménes cannot be impeached for good faith with us.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
